  "synopsis": "Thorfinn has earned a notable reputation as one of the most skilled warriors in the group of mercenaries under the leadership of the cunning Askeladd. Despite being the son of one of the Vikings' greatest fighters, Thorfinn's motivations for joining the crew are not for the spoils of war, but rather to seek revenge for the great tragedy inflicted upon his family by killing Askeladd in a fair fight. Though he is not yet capable of accomplishing his ultimate goal, Thorfinn continues to hone his skills on the battlefield alongside the warlike Danes who derive pleasure from their killing sprees. In a twist of fate, Askeladd devises a daring plan after learning that the Danish prince, Canute, has been captured. The success of his plan will determine the next King of England and drastically alter the fates of Thorfinn, Canute, and himself. Set in 11th-century Europe, Vinland Saga exposes a world of senseless violence, insanity, and injustice – a dream come true for those who revel in battle but a living nightmare for those who must endure it.",
